# The day as each one lives it (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): calls and remarks to no one, by where they are in
# their day (before work, at it, done, a day off), the kind of day (market, Restday, a festival) as it falls on them,
# the hour, and their errands, the road and the watch. Then how they are: hurt, grieving, hungry, roofless, in debt,
# flush. Barks have cooldowns, so a habit shows without wearing thin.

## The working day

rule day_late_for_work
when concept=bark shift=before here.time=dawn
cooldown 12h
say Late. Late, late, late. | If I run I'll make it. | Not a crumb of breakfast. Again. | Where's my other boot? Where's my other boot?

rule day_off_to_work
when concept=bark shift=before
cooldown 12h
say Another day, another #money#. | Right. Off we go. | #work.capitalize# won't do itself. | Chin up, tail up, off we go.

rule day_done
when concept=bark shift=after
cooldown 12h
say Done! Done for the day. | That's me finished. | #home.capitalize#, and my feet up. | Not one more thing. Not today.

rule day_done_tired
when concept=bark shift=after tired=yes
cooldown 12h
say Every bone. Every single bone. | I could sleep standing. | Straight to #bed#. Straight there. | Carry me home, somebody. Anybody.

rule day_day_off
when concept=bark shift=day_off
cooldown 12h
say No #work# today. Not a stroke. | What shall I do with myself? | Lovely. Lovely, lovely day off. | A whole day, and nobody wanting anything.

rule day_working_hard
when concept=bark working=yes shift=during tired=yes
cooldown 6h
say How long till dusk? | My back's done in. | Keep at it. Keep at it. | Nearly there. Nearly. That's what I said an hour ago.

rule day_working_restday
when concept=bark working=yes here.day=rest
cooldown 1d
say Working on Restday. The gods'll have words. | Everyone at chapel but me. | Somebody's got to. | Rest, they call it. Ha.

rule day_working_festival
when concept=bark working=yes here.day=festival
cooldown 1d
say Everyone feasting but me. | Save me a cake, somebody! | I can smell the roasting from here. | Listen to them out there. Somebody's having fun.

rule day_working_market
when concept=bark working=yes here.day=market role!=merchant
cooldown 1d
say Market day, and I'm stuck at #work#. | Can't even get to the stalls. | Somebody buy me a pie. | All the best cheese'll be gone by the time I'm out.

rule day_devout_restday
when concept=bark here.day=rest piety=devout
cooldown 1d
say Chapel at noon. Don't be late. | A blessed Restday to you all. | Rest, and give thanks. | The Bright One rested once. So can you.

rule day_festival_merry
when concept=bark here.day=festival humour=merry here.festival
cooldown 6h
say Happy #here.festival#! | #here.festival#! Have you had a cake yet? | Dance with me! It's #here.festival#! | #here.festival#, and not a sad face allowed!

rule day_festival_poor
when concept=bark here.day=festival wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say Feasts are for them as can pay. | All this food and I can't touch it. | A festival. Lovely. For some. | I'll feast on the smell, then.

## The hours

rule day_dawn_old
when concept=bark here.time=dawn stage=old
cooldown 1d
say Up before the birds. Always am. | At my age you don't sleep, you wait. | Another morning. Thank the gods. | The cocks are late. I'm not.

rule day_dusk_lamps
when concept=bark here.time=dusk here.place=street
cooldown 12h
say Lamps soon. | Getting dark early. | Home before the light goes. | There goes the sun. Supper, then.

rule day_night_street
when concept=bark here.time=night here.place=street stage!=young
cooldown 12h
say Should be abed. | Dark as a pocket out here. | Mind the gutter. Mind the... ow. | Who moved the step? Somebody's moved the step.

rule day_night_nervy
when concept=bark here.time=night temper=nervy here.weather!=indoors
cooldown 12h
say Who's there? ... Nobody. Nobody. | I don't like the dark. Never have. | Was that a step? That was a step. | Walk faster. Don't look back. Walk faster.

rule day_night_tavern
when concept=bark here.time=night here.place=tavern
cooldown 6h
say One more. Just the one. | Who's buying? Not me. | Another song! Another! | Keeper! Keeper, my jar's empty and so am I.

## Errands, the road, the watch

rule day_errand_letter
when concept=bark errand=letter
cooldown 6h
say Letter. Letter for... where is that door? | Mind out, letter to deliver. | Now who was this for? | Third door past the well, they said. Which well?

rule day_errand_caravan
when concept=bark errand=caravan
cooldown 6h
say The caravan won't wait! | Coming, coming! | Is that them gone already? | Hold the carts! Hold them!

rule day_errand_goods
when concept=bark errand=goods
cooldown 6h
say Mind your backs! Coming through! | Heavy, this. Mind out. | Watch your toes! | Make way, make way, it's heavier than it looks.

rule day_errand_order
when concept=bark errand=order
cooldown 6h
say An order to fetch. Don't stop me. | They wanted it yesterday. | Quick, quick. | If it's not ready I'll wait on the step till it is.

rule day_errand_wedding
when concept=bark errand=wedding
cooldown 6h
say A wedding! Have you seen the bride? | Off to a wedding. Do I look all right? | Flowers! I forgot the flowers. | Is my collar straight? Somebody tell me my collar's straight.

rule day_errand_funeral
when concept=bark errand=funeral
cooldown 6h
say *walks with head bowed* | They were good folk. | Walk soft. There's been a death. | Bright One keep them.

rule day_travelling
when concept=bark travelling=yes
cooldown 6h
say Long road yet. | My paws. My poor paws. | Is it far now? It's always far. | One more hill. There's always one more hill.

rule day_watch_night
when concept=bark on_watch=yes here.time=night
cooldown 3h
say All's well! | Who goes there? | Keep to the lamps, now. | Home, the lot of you. It's late.

rule day_watch_day
when concept=bark on_watch=yes here.time=dawn|day|dusk
cooldown 3h
say Move along, now. | Keep it civil, now. | Eyes open. Always. | No running in the street. You. Yes, you.

## How they are

rule day_rich
when concept=bark wealth=rich here.place=street|market
cooldown 1d
say Out of the way, if you please. | Such crowds. | Where is that boy with my parcels? | One can hardly move for people.

rule day_heights
when concept=bark quarter=heights here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say One does so tire of the Commons' smell. | Ghastly crowds today. | Mind the hem. This was dear. | Somebody fetch me a chair. These steps.

rule day_sump
when concept=bark quarter=sump here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say Up to the ankles again. | Sump water. Sump everything. | The Heights never smell this. | Mind the third step. It's not there.

rule day_hungry
when concept=bark hungry=yes
cooldown 6h
say #hungry.capitalize#. | Spare a crust? Anyone? | I can smell bread. Torture. | My belly's growling at strangers.

rule day_homeless
when concept=bark homeless=yes
priority 1
cooldown 6h
say Anywhere dry. Anywhere at all. | Spare a corner? | Another night out, then. | A door. Just a door to shut. That's all.

rule day_on_dole
when concept=bark on_dole=yes
cooldown 1d
say Parish loaf again. | Queue's longer every week. | Thank the gods for the dole, I suppose. | Same bread, same line, same faces.

rule day_owes
when concept=bark owes=yes stage=adult|old
cooldown 1d
say If anyone asks, I'm not here. | Pay it back Restday. Restday for sure. | How did it get so much? | Don't look round. Just walk.

rule day_hurt_light
when concept=bark injured=light
cooldown 6h
say *winces* | Mind the paw. | Still #hurt#. It'll pass. | Ow. Ow. Stupid step.

rule day_mourning_friend
when concept=bark mourning=friend
cooldown 12h
say They'd have liked this weather. | Gone. Just like that. | I keep seeing them in the crowd. | We were going to go fishing. We kept saying.

rule day_widowed
when concept=bark widowed=yes
cooldown 1d
say We used to walk here. | Quiet, without them. | I still say goodnight to the empty side of the bed. | They'd have laughed at that. They laughed at everything.

rule day_fought
when concept=bark fought=yes
cooldown 6h
say Let them try again. Let them. | My jaw. My poor jaw. | Should've seen it coming. | Still shaking. Still shaking, look.

rule day_fighting
when concept=bark fighting=yes
priority 3
say Come on, then! | Is that all? | You'll regret that! | Stand still and fight!

rule day_apprentice
when concept=bark apprentice=yes working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Yes, master. Coming, master. | Sweep, fetch, carry. Sweep, fetch, carry. | One day it'll be my shop. | I did it right! I think I did it right.

rule day_master
when concept=bark master=yes working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Not like that. Like this! | Where's that apprentice got to? | In my day we learnt by watching. | Again. From the start. Slowly.

rule day_ambitious
when concept=bark drive=ambitious working=yes
cooldown 1d
say One day this'll all be mine. | Faster. There's money in faster. | Mark me: I'll be someone. | Twice the work, twice the coin. That's sums.

rule day_chatty_alone
when concept=bark self.talk=chatty
cooldown 1d
say Talking to myself again. Best company. | Nobody to talk to. Well, there's me. | Where's everyone gone? | I'll just say this out loud, then. Nobody minds.

rule day_dry
when concept=bark humour=dry here.weather=rain|storm|fog
cooldown 1d
say Lovely day for it. | Glorious. Truly glorious. | Just how I like it. | Weather for ducks. And me, apparently.
